---
import Layout from '../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="What's Your Audience Worth? | Redefining Retirement"
  description="Curious what your audience could actually be worth as an email list? This free calculator shows you the number — and what you're risking by not having one."
  type="website"
>
  <article class="section">
    <div class="container narrow">

      <!-- ── HERO ─────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
      <header class="article-header">
        <span class="tag">Free Calculator</span>
        <h1 class="article-title">What's Your Audience Worth?</h1>
        <p class="article-deck">
          Curious what your following could actually be worth as an email list? So was I, so I built this.
        </p>
      </header>

      <!-- Hero image — src swapped in once image is approved -->
      <div class="hero-img-wrap">
        <img
          src="/tools/audience-worth-hero.jpg"
          alt=""
          class="hero-img"
          aria-hidden="true"
          onerror="this.parentElement.style.display='none'"
        />
      </div>

      <!-- ── INTRO COPY ─────────────────────────────────────────── -->
      <div class="prose intro-prose">
        <p>I've built a few email lists over the years, so I know roughly what they're worth. But what kept catching my eye was all these creators out there — big YouTube followings, solid TikTok numbers — with zero email list. None.</p>
        <p>And I started thinking: do they even know what they're sitting on? Or more to the point — what they're <em>risking</em> by not having it?</p>
        <p>So I built this. Answer a few quick questions about your audience, and I'll show you roughly what it could be worth as an email list — the kind of number that's hard to un-see once you've seen it.</p>
        <p class="jerry-line"><em>You know the line from Jerry Maguire. Stop wondering. Let's see your number.</em></p>
      </div>

      <!-- ── CALCULATOR ────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
      <div class="calc-card">
        <form id="calc-form" novalidate>

          <div class="field">
            <label for="niche">What's your topic, niche, or profession?</label>
            <input
              type="text"
              id="niche"
              name="niche"
              placeholder="e.g. Fitness Coach, Personal Finance, Productivity Coach, Parenting Blogger"
              autocomplete="off"
            />
          </div>

          <div class="field">
            <label>Do you have a social media audience?</label>
            <div class="radio-group">
              <label class="radio-opt">
                <input type="radio" name="has_social" value="yes" />
                Yes
              </label>
              <label class="radio-opt">
                <input type="radio" name="has_social" value="no" />
                Not yet
              </label>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="field conditional hidden" id="social-size-wrap">
            <label for="social_size">Approx. total social followers (all platforms combined)</label>
            <select id="social_size" name="social_size">
              <option value="">Pick a range</option>
              <option value="under-1k">Less than 1,000</option>
              <option value="1k-5k">1,000 – 5,000</option>
              <option value="5k-10k">5,000 – 10,000</option>
              <option value="10k-plus">10,000+</option>
            </select>
          </div>

          <div class="field">
            <label>Do you have a newsletter or email list?</label>
            <div class="radio-group">
              <label class="radio-opt">
                <input type="radio" name="has_email" value="yes" />
                Yes
              </label>
              <label class="radio-opt">
                <input type="radio" name="has_email" value="no" />
                No
              </label>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="field conditional hidden" id="email-size-wrap">
            <label for="email_size">How many subscribers do you have?</label>
            <select id="email_size" name="email_size">
              <option value="">Pick a range</option>
              <option value="under-1k">Less than 1,000</option>
              <option value="1k-5k">1,000 – 5,000</option>
              <option value="5k-10k">5,000 – 10,000</option>
              <option value="10k-plus">10,000+</option>
            </select>
          </div>

          <div class="field">
            <label>
              Monetization paths you'd want to explore
              <span class="field-note">— select all that apply</span>
            </label>
            <div class="check-group">
              <label class="check-opt">
                <input type="checkbox" name="monetization" value="service" />
                <span>
                  Service-Based Offers
                  <span class="check-desc">Coaching, consulting, or fully managed done-for-you work</span>
                </span>
              </label>
              <label class="check-opt">
                <input type="checkbox" name="monetization" value="recurring" />
                <span>
                  Recurring Revenue
                  <span class="check-desc">Subscriptions, sponsorships, and affiliate income</span>
                </span>
              </label>
              <label class="check-opt">
                <input type="checkbox" name="monetization" value="education" />
                <span>
                  Education-Based Offers
                  <span class="check-desc">Courses, workshops, and coaching programs</span>
                </span>
              </label>
              <label class="check-opt">
                <input type="checkbox" name="monetization" value="digital" />
                <span>
                  Additional Revenue Streams
                  <span class="check-desc">Digital products, sponsored content, and merch</span>
                </span>
              </label>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="form-error hidden" id="form-error" role="alert"></div>

          <button type="submit" class="btn btn-calc">Show Me The Money →</button>
        </form>
      </div>

      <!-- ── RESULTS (injected by JS) ──────────────────────────────── -->
      <div id="results" class="results hidden" aria-live="polite"></div>

      <!-- ── CTAS ──────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
      <div class="ctas-section">

        <div class="cta-divider"><span>What now?</span></div>

        <!-- CTA 1: Beehiiv signup -->
        <div class="cta-card cta-beehiiv">
          <div class="cta-card__label">Ready to start?</div>
          <h2>Here's where I moved mine.</h2>
          <p>I landed on Beehiiv — strong analytics, a built-in referral system, and they don't take a cut of your paid subscribers. I'm not going anywhere.</p>
          <p>Use my link and the code <strong class="coupon">MIGRATE</strong> for 20% off your first three months.</p>
          <a
            href="https://www.beehiiv.com?via=MIGRATE"
            class="btn"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
          >
            Start on Beehiiv →
          </a>
          <p class="cta-note">Free plan available. Affiliate link — I earn a small commission at no cost to you.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- CTA 2: First 50 Subscribers quick-start (free) -->
        <div class="cta-card cta-quickstart">
          <div class="cta-card__label">Free guide</div>
          <h2>Here's how to close that gap — on me.</h2>
          <p>The exact 3-step plan to get your first 50 subscribers in a week, starting from zero. Same steps I'd use myself. No fluff, no paywall.</p>
          <div class="cta-form">
            <div data-beehiiv-form-id="c7512ec6-96c4-497a-851a-3d8b9f59c108"></div>
            <script is:inline async src="https://subscribe-forms.beehiiv.com/v3/loader.js" data-beehiiv-form="c7512ec6-96c4-497a-851a-3d8b9f59c108"></script>
            <script is:inline type="text/javascript" async src="https://subscribe-forms.beehiiv.com/attribution.js"></script>
          </div>
        </div>

      </div>

    </div>
  </article>

  <script>
    // ── BENCHMARKS ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    // Source: Neil Patel study of 2,501 marketers
    const SOCIAL_PER_1K = 79;
    const EMAIL_PER_1K  = 582;

    // Income range: low (~30% of avg) and high (~180% of avg)
    const RANGE_LOW  = 0.30;
    const RANGE_HIGH = 1.80;

    const MIDPOINTS: Record<string, number> = {
      'under-1k': 500,
      '1k-5k':    2500,
      '5k-10k':   7500,
      '10k-plus': 15000,
    };

    const MONO_LABELS: Record<string, string> = {
      service:   'Service-Based Offers',
      recurring: 'Recurring Revenue',
      education: 'Education-Based Offers',
      digital:   'Additional Revenue Streams',
    };

    const MONO_COPY: Record<string, string> = {
      service:
        'High-ticket, low-volume — the sweet spot for email. A list of 500 engaged subscribers and one offer at $500 is $2,500 if just 1% buy. The math works at small scale in a way it never does on social.',
      recurring:
        'The compounding play. The difference between a one-time sale and recurring income is the difference between starting over every month and not having to.',
      education:
        'High-margin and scales well — teach what you know once, sell it indefinitely. An email list is how you fill it without spending money on ads.',
      digital:
        'Builds slowly but compounds. Best paired with a higher-ticket model so you\'re not depending on volume alone.',
    };

    const MONO_ITEMS: Record<string, { label: string; desc: string }[]> = {
      service: [
        { label: 'Done by You ($)', desc: 'Coaching, consulting, or small digital services you deliver yourself.' },
        { label: 'Done with You ($$)', desc: 'Hands-on mentorship or group coaching programs.' },
        { label: 'Done for You ($$$)', desc: 'Fully managed services where you or your team execute for clients.' },
      ],
      recurring: [
        { label: 'Subscriptions', desc: 'Premium content, exclusive reports, or a private community.' },
        { label: 'Partnerships & Ads', desc: 'Sponsors or ads placed in your newsletter.' },
        { label: 'Affiliate Marketing', desc: 'Recommend tools or products you use and earn a commission.' },
      ],
      education: [
        { label: 'Courses', desc: 'Teach what you know through an online course or workshop.' },
        { label: 'Coaching', desc: 'One-on-one or group sessions to help subscribers reach a goal.' },
      ],
      digital: [
        { label: 'Digital Products', desc: 'Templates, checklists, or ebooks.' },
        { label: 'Sponsored Content', desc: 'Get paid to feature relevant products or services in your newsletter.' },
        { label: 'Physical Merchandise', desc: 'Print-on-demand branded products — t-shirts, hats, mugs, and more.' },
      ],
    };

    const MILESTONES = [500, 1000, 5000, 10000];

    // ── FORMATTING ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    function fmtRange(count: number): string {
      const low  = Math.max(50, Math.round((count / 1000) * EMAIL_PER_1K * RANGE_LOW  / 50) * 50);
      const high = Math.round((count / 1000) * EMAIL_PER_1K * RANGE_HIGH / 50) * 50;
      return '$' + low.toLocaleString() + ' – $' + high.toLocaleString() + '/mo';
    }

    function fmtMid(count: number): string {
      const mid = Math.max(50, Math.round((count / 1000) * EMAIL_PER_1K / 50) * 50);
      return '$' + mid.toLocaleString() + '/mo';
    }

    function fmtSocial(count: number): string {
      const val = Math.max(10, Math.round((count / 1000) * SOCIAL_PER_1K / 10) * 10);
      return '$' + val.toLocaleString() + '/mo';
    }

    function fmtCount(n: number): string {
      return n.toLocaleString();
    }

    // ── SHOW/HIDE ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    function show(el: HTMLElement | null) { el?.classList.remove('hidden'); }
    function hide(el: HTMLElement | null) { el?.classList.add('hidden'); }

    // ── CONDITIONAL FIELDS ────────────────────────────────────────────
    const socialWrap = document.getElementById('social-size-wrap') as HTMLElement;
    const emailWrap  = document.getElementById('email-size-wrap')  as HTMLElement;

    document.querySelectorAll('[name="has_social"]').forEach((radio) => {
      radio.addEventListener('change', () => {
        const r = radio as HTMLInputElement;
        if (r.value === 'yes') { show(socialWrap); }
        else { hide(socialWrap); (document.getElementById('social_size') as HTMLSelectElement).value = ''; }
      });
    });

    document.querySelectorAll('[name="has_email"]').forEach((radio) => {
      radio.addEventListener('change', () => {
        const r = radio as HTMLInputElement;
        if (r.value === 'yes') { show(emailWrap); }
        else { hide(emailWrap); (document.getElementById('email_size') as HTMLSelectElement).value = ''; }
      });
    });

    // ── FORM SUBMIT ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    document.getElementById('calc-form')!.addEventListener('submit', (e) => {
      e.preventDefault();

      const niche      = (document.getElementById('niche') as HTMLInputElement).value.trim() || 'your niche';
      const hasSocial  = (document.querySelector('[name="has_social"]:checked') as HTMLInputElement | null)?.value;
      const socialSize = (document.getElementById('social_size') as HTMLSelectElement).value;
      const hasEmail   = (document.querySelector('[name="has_email"]:checked') as HTMLInputElement | null)?.value;
      const emailSize  = (document.getElementById('email_size') as HTMLSelectElement).value;
      const monoPaths  = [...document.querySelectorAll('[name="monetization"]:checked')]
        .map((el) => (el as HTMLInputElement).value);

      const errorEl = document.getElementById('form-error')!;
      if (!hasSocial || !hasEmail) {
        errorEl.textContent = 'Please answer all the yes/no questions above.';
        show(errorEl); return;
      }
      if (hasSocial === 'yes' && !socialSize) {
        errorEl.textContent = 'Please select your approximate social audience size.';
        show(errorEl); return;
      }
      if (hasEmail === 'yes' && !emailSize) {
        errorEl.textContent = 'Please select your approximate subscriber count.';
        show(errorEl); return;
      }
      hide(errorEl);
      errorEl.textContent = '';

      const socialCount = hasSocial === 'yes' ? (MIDPOINTS[socialSize] ?? 0) : 0;
      const emailCount  = hasEmail  === 'yes' ? (MIDPOINTS[emailSize]  ?? 0) : 0;

      renderResults({ niche, hasSocial, hasEmail, socialCount, emailCount, monoPaths });

      setTimeout(() => {
        document.getElementById('results')!.scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'smooth', block: 'start' });
      }, 80);
    });

    // ── RENDER ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    interface CalcData {
      niche: string; hasSocial: string; hasEmail: string;
      socialCount: number; emailCount: number; monoPaths: string[];
    }

    function renderResults(d: CalcData) {
      const resultsEl = document.getElementById('results')!;

      // Honest note
      const honestNote = `
        <div class="honest-note">
          <strong>A quick disclaimer:</strong> These are estimates based on industry averages — not a guarantee of what you'll earn. Your actual results depend on your niche, your offer, and what you do with the list. Nothing here is financial advice. Think of it as a benchmark, not a contract.
        </div>
      `;

      // Opener
      const openerHTML = `<p class="result-opener-line">You asked for it. Here it is.</p>`;

      // Headline number + situation + narrative — 4 scenarios
      let headlineHTML = '';
      let situationHTML = '';
      let narrativeHTML = '';

      if (d.hasSocial === 'yes' && d.hasEmail === 'no') {
        headlineHTML = `
          <div class="result-headline-block">
            <p class="rh-label">Your ${fmtCount(d.socialCount)} followers — as an email list — could be worth</p>
            <p class="rh-number">${fmtMid(d.socialCount)}</p>
            <p class="rh-range">Realistic range: ${fmtRange(d.socialCount)}</p>
          </div>
        `;
        situationHTML = `
          <div class="result-section">
            <p class="result-section-label">Your starting point</p>
            <div class="prose result-prose">
              <p>You've got <strong>${fmtCount(d.socialCount)} social followers</strong> in ${d.niche} and no email list yet. Your social audience is worth roughly <strong>${fmtSocial(d.socialCount)}</strong> in estimated platform value — but that number lives on someone else's server, subject to someone else's algorithm.</p>
              <p>The same audience, migrated to email? Closer to ${fmtMid(d.socialCount)} a month on average — and it's yours to keep.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        `;
        const gap = Math.max(0, Math.round(((d.socialCount / 1000) * EMAIL_PER_1K - (d.socialCount / 1000) * SOCIAL_PER_1K) / 50) * 50);
        narrativeHTML = `
          <div class="result-section">
            <p class="result-section-label">What this means</p>
            <div class="prose result-prose">
              <p>You've done the hard part — built an audience who pays attention. The gap between where you are and where you could be isn't effort. It's infrastructure. You need a place to send people that you own outright.</p>
              <p>Every day without a list, you're building on rented land. Platforms have changed their rules before. They'll do it again. The list is the thing that doesn't disappear when they do.</p>
              ${gap > 100 ? `<p>The monthly gap between your current social value and your email list potential: roughly <strong>$${gap.toLocaleString()}</strong>. It grows every time you add a subscriber.</p>` : ''}
            </div>
          </div>
        `;
      }

      else if (d.hasSocial === 'yes' && d.hasEmail === 'yes') {
        headlineHTML = `
          <div class="result-headline-block">
            <p class="rh-label">Your ${fmtCount(d.emailCount)}-subscriber list in ${d.niche} is worth</p>
            <p class="rh-number">${fmtMid(d.emailCount)}</p>
            <p class="rh-range">Realistic range: ${fmtRange(d.emailCount)}</p>
          </div>
        `;
        situationHTML = `
          <div class="result-section">
            <p class="result-section-label">Your starting point</p>
            <div class="prose result-prose">
              <p>You've got <strong>${fmtCount(d.emailCount)} email subscribers</strong> and <strong>${fmtCount(d.socialCount)} social followers</strong> in ${d.niche}. You're already ahead of most creators — you have an asset you own, not just an audience you're renting.</p>
              <p>Your social reach represents additional upside: if those ${fmtCount(d.socialCount)} followers were on your list too, you'd be looking at roughly ${fmtMid(d.socialCount)} a month from that segment alone.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        `;
        narrativeHTML = `
          <div class="result-section">
            <p class="result-section-label">What this means</p>
            <div class="prose result-prose">
              <p>You've done the smart thing. The next move is two-pronged: keep migrating your social following onto the list, and make sure you're actually monetizing the subscribers you already have.</p>
              <p>Most creators with a list your size are under-monetizing it. The numbers below show what's possible at your current count — and where the ceiling is if you keep growing.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        `;
      }

      else if (d.hasSocial === 'no' && d.hasEmail === 'yes') {
        headlineHTML = `
          <div class="result-headline-block">
            <p class="rh-label">Your ${fmtCount(d.emailCount)}-subscriber list in ${d.niche} is worth</p>
            <p class="rh-number">${fmtMid(d.emailCount)}</p>
            <p class="rh-range">Realistic range: ${fmtRange(d.emailCount)}</p>
          </div>
        `;
        situationHTML = `
          <div class="result-section">
            <p class="result-section-label">Your starting point</p>
            <div class="prose result-prose">
              <p>You've got <strong>${fmtCount(d.emailCount)} email subscribers</strong> in ${d.niche} — and you built the right thing first. No algorithm between you and your audience. No platform that can pull the rug.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        `;
        narrativeHTML = `
          <div class="result-section">
            <p class="result-section-label">What this means</p>
            <div class="prose result-prose">
              <p>You've already made the move most creators never make. The next unlock is adding a content-discovery layer — YouTube, social, SEO — that feeds more people into the list you already own.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        `;
      }

      else {
        headlineHTML = `
          <div class="result-headline-block zero">
            <p class="rh-label">Starting from zero in ${d.niche}.</p>
            <p class="rh-number">That's actually fine.</p>
            <p class="rh-range">Here's what the numbers look like once you're moving.</p>
          </div>
        `;
        situationHTML = `
          <div class="result-section">
            <p class="result-section-label">Your starting point</p>
            <div class="prose result-prose">
              <p>No social audience yet, no email list yet — just you and ${d.niche}. You don't have bad habits to undo, no sunk cost keeping you on the wrong platform, and no existing audience scattered across a dozen places.</p>
              <p>Starting clean is an advantage most people don't recognize until they've already made the mistakes.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        `;
        narrativeHTML = `
          <div class="result-section">
            <p class="result-section-label">What this means</p>
            <div class="prose result-prose">
              <p>The hardest part is sending the first email. After that, every subscriber makes the list more valuable — and unlike a social following, you own them. The milestone table below shows what you're working toward.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        `;
      }

      // Milestone table
      const MILESTONE_NOTES: Record<number, string> = {
        500:   'First offers, list getting established',
        1000:  'Affiliate + service income starting to compound',
        5000:  'Sponsorships, paid tiers, multiple streams possible',
        10000: 'Full monetization mix, serious recurring potential',
      };

      const milestoneRows = MILESTONES.map((m) => `
        <tr>
          <td class="ms-count">${fmtCount(m)}</td>
          <td class="ms-mid">${fmtMid(m)}</td>
          <td class="ms-range">${fmtRange(m)}</td>
          <td class="ms-note hide-mobile">${MILESTONE_NOTES[m]}</td>
        </tr>
      `).join('');

      const milestoneHTML = `
        <div class="result-section">
          <p class="result-section-label">Subscriber milestones — what the numbers look like</p>
          <table class="ms-table">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th>Subscribers</th>
                <th>Avg est.</th>
                <th>Range</th>
                <th class="hide-mobile">What drives it</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>${milestoneRows}</tbody>
          </table>
          <p class="ms-footnote">Based on a Neil Patel study of 2,501 marketers (avg: $582/month per 1,000 email subscribers). Range reflects early-stage vs. well-monetized lists. Your results depend on your offer, engagement, and niche.</p>
        </div>
      `;

      // Monetization paths
      let monoHTML = '';
      if (d.monoPaths.length > 0) {
        monoHTML = `
          <div class="result-section result-section--alt">
            <p class="result-section-label">Your selected monetization paths</p>
            <div class="mono-list">
              ${d.monoPaths.map((path) => `
                <div class="mono-item">
                  <p class="mono-label">${MONO_LABELS[path]}</p>
                  <p>${MONO_COPY[path]}</p>
                  <ul class="mono-sublist">
                    ${MONO_ITEMS[path].map((item) => `
                      <li><strong>${item.label}:</strong> ${item.desc}</li>
                    `).join('')}
                  </ul>
                </div>
              `).join('')}
            </div>
          </div>
        `;
      }

      // Closing
      const closingHTML = `
        <div class="result-section result-closing">
          <div class="prose result-prose">
            <p><em>I built my list before I needed it. I wish someone had shown me this number sooner.</em></p>
            <p><em>Now you've got it. The rest is up to you.</em></p>
            <p class="closing-sig">— Corey</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      `;

      resultsEl.innerHTML = `
        <div class="results-card">
          ${honestNote}
          <div class="result-opener">${openerHTML}</div>
          ${headlineHTML}
          ${situationHTML}
          ${narrativeHTML}
          ${milestoneHTML}
          ${monoHTML}
          ${closingHTML}
        </div>
      `;

      show(resultsEl);
    }
  </script>

  <style is:global>
    .narrow { max-width: 720px; }
    .hidden { display: none !important; }

    /* ── HERO ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
    .article-title {
      font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 4vw, 2.8rem);
      color: var(--text);
      margin-bottom: 1rem;
      line-height: 1.1;
    }

    .article-deck {
      color: var(--text-muted);
      font-size: 1.1rem;
      max-width: 640px;
      line-height: 1.65;
      margin-bottom: 0;
    }

    /* Hero image */
    .hero-img-wrap {
      margin: 2rem 0;
      border-radius: var(--radius);
      overflow: hidden;
    }

    .hero-img {
      width: 100%;
      height: 360px;
      object-fit: cover;
      object-position: center top;
      display: block;
    }

    /* Intro prose */
    .intro-prose {
      margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
    }

    .jerry-line {
      margin-top: 0.5rem;
      margin-bottom: 0 !important;
    }

    /* ── CALCULATOR ────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
    .calc-card {
      background: var(--bg-subtle);
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: var(--radius);
      padding: 2rem;
      margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
    }

    .field { margin-bottom: 1.75rem; }
    .field:last-of-type { margin-bottom: 0; }

    .field > label:first-child {
      display: block;
      font-weight: 600;
      font-size: 0.95rem;
      color: var(--text);
      margin-bottom: 0.65rem;
      line-height: 1.4;
    }

    .field-note {
      font-weight: 400;
      color: var(--text-light);
      font-size: 0.85rem;
    }

    .conditional {
      padding-left: 1.25rem;
